{"kind":"request","text":"GW-1: the installed-screen gateway allows the read minimum. NF-A1 (e240c288) found that applicationGatewayRoute refuses any read with ?atLeast= (application-gateway.ts:64), so followReceipt fails and every hosted browser join through an installed screen ends 'No answer came back that could be trusted'. Ruling: every read route that takes a minimum, one rule. The client, the sandbox Worker and the scope Worker share the route. Builder lane, next after the current one.","body":{"conditions":"1. applicationGatewayRoute allows exactly one atLeast query parameter, in the read-minimum encoding (minimumPath), on every read route that takes a minimum: summary, history, items, application-projection and entries. Any other parameter, a second atLeast, or a malformed value is refused as today. Write routes are unchanged. 2. application-gateway.test.ts: per route, one case that allows a well-formed atLeast and one that refuses a malformed or doubled one, with a named red (the rule without atLeast fails the allow cases). 3. A client case: followReceipt through applicationScreenTransport reads the entry with its minimum and settles a join as recorded. 4. The CB/screen notes or the gateway note name the rule. 5. Gate once, review, land; the planner deploys the sandbox and the room Workers with a rate read, then issues a fresh invitation for a hosted NF-7 rerun.","target_head":"356fcd1175e036e1a813d3190f506e54eac3f79b","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}